Changed render_dot(): rankdir=TB (top-to-bottom) instead of LR, and node [shape=circle] instead of box. Since edge A -> B means "A depends on B", rankdir=TB naturally puts folders with no incoming dependency edges at the top and their dependencies cascading down.

One thing to flag: Graphviz's circle shape only stays a true circle for short labels — long folder names will stretch it into an oval. Say the word if you want fixedsize=true (and a fixed width) to force perfect circles regardless of label length.


